USB Ethernet (rtos/cherryusb/net): the RTL8152 and ASIX class driver objects get external
linkage like cdc_ecm_class_driver/cdc_ncm_class_driver already have, so the image's own class
table (net/usbnet_classes.c; the RTEMS link has no .usbh_class_info section) can name them.

diff --git a/class/vendor/net/usbh_asix.c b/class/vendor/net/usbh_asix.c
index 545f8cc..95444c1 100644
--- a/class/vendor/net/usbh_asix.c
+++ b/class/vendor/net/usbh_asix.c
@@ -795,7 +795,7 @@ static const uint16_t asix_id_table[][2] = {
     { 0, 0 },
 };
 
-static const struct usbh_class_driver asix_class_driver = {
+const struct usbh_class_driver asix_class_driver = {
     .driver_name = "asix",
     .connect = usbh_asix_connect,
     .disconnect = usbh_asix_disconnect
